# §15.4: the app signing key is generated and held by the owner locally and
# must never be committed. Copy this file to `keystore.properties` (already
# gitignored) at the repo root, fill in the real values, and Gradle picks it
# up automatically for release builds (androidApp/build.gradle.kts).
#
# Generate the key once, per §15.4 step 1, e.g.:
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore skyward-release.jks -alias skyward \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#
# The same key signs both the `foss` and `play` release variants (§15.4 step 3)
# — do not generate a second key for Play; upload a *copy* of this one via
# PEPK (see RELEASE.md) so both stores share one signing identity.
#
# storeFile may be relative to the repo root or absolute.
storeFile=/absolute/or/repo-root-relative/path/to/skyward-release.jks
storePassword=changeme
keyAlias=skyward
keyPassword=changeme
